linux-galaxyxr (5.10.240.13~26.10.1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * linux-image ships only the complete device tree of each board
    revision, anorakp-samsung-xrvst2-rev22.dtb and -rev25.dtb. The base
    trees and the board overlays are gone: nothing merges them at boot
    any more.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:42:55 +0000

linux-galaxyxr (5.10.240.12~26.10.1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Keep the EFI zboot image's .data section in the file: systemd-stub
    does not zero a section without file data, so the decompressor failed
    when the kernel was started from a unified kernel image.
  * Add a complete device tree per board revision,
    anorakp-samsung-xrvst2-rev22.dtb and -rev25.dtb: the base tree with
    the board overlay applied, "samsung,xrvst2-revNN" as the first
    compatible, and the nodes the Android bootloader adds at boot. They
    are what a unified kernel image carries; xrboot-kernel-install 4
    builds one from them.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:28:46 +0000

linux-galaxyxr (5.10.240.11~26.10.1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Run the kernel install hooks from a dpkg trigger, at the end of the
    dpkg run: installed in the same run, dracut and xrboot-kernel-install
    were not configured yet when the hooks ran.
  * Fix a kernel panic when unloading the sec_qc_qcom_reboot_reason or
    sec_qc_qcom_wdt_core module (a NULL dereference of its driver data).

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:33:25 +0000

linux-galaxyxr (5.10.240.10~26.10.1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Power USB devices that are attached at boot. Drop the USB notifier's
    10 second boot delay: it skipped the Type-C VBUS booster, so a USB
    drive plugged in at boot was never powered and could not be the root.
  * linux-image-galaxyxr recommends linux-firmware instead of depending on
    it: the Galaxy XR's own firmware comes from galaxyxr-firmware, so small
    systems can leave out the firmware for other hardware.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:32:42 +0000

